1
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,710
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:07,774 --> 00:00:09,344
A supermarket trolley!

3
00:00:10,934 --> 00:00:13,134
Which material would you choose to make it?

4
00:00:14,704 --> 00:00:15,784
One, glass.

5
00:00:17,344 --> 00:00:18,314
Two, metal.

6
00:00:19,894 --> 00:00:21,074
Three, fabric.

7
00:00:23,224 --> 00:00:24,734
Hold on to your answer!

8
00:00:26,956 --> 00:00:28,416
You against the Buddies!

9
00:00:28,696 --> 00:00:29,916
Lock in first.

10
00:00:30,186 --> 00:00:31,996
One finger for every point.

11
00:00:32,286 --> 00:00:34,706
A little mynah is hiding in this video.

12
00:00:34,986 --> 00:00:36,186
Can you spot it?

13
00:00:36,764 --> 00:00:38,064
Today you'll learn:

14
00:00:38,267 --> 00:00:40,077
Objects have purposes.

15
00:00:40,273 --> 00:00:42,213
Properties decide uses.

16
00:00:42,416 --> 00:00:44,046
Why a trolley is metal.

17
00:00:44,693 --> 00:00:45,633
Are you ready?

18
00:00:46,073 --> 00:00:46,843
Three!

19
00:00:47,223 --> 00:00:47,883
Two!

20
00:00:48,253 --> 00:00:48,903
One!

21
00:00:49,323 --> 00:00:50,043
Go!

22
00:00:50,922 --> 00:00:52,852
First: what is a trolley for?

23
00:00:53,142 --> 00:00:54,252
Look closer.

24
00:00:54,905 --> 00:00:56,515
A bag of rice goes in.

25
00:00:57,135 --> 00:00:58,045
Bottles.

26
00:00:58,715 --> 00:00:59,485
Tins.

27
00:01:00,045 --> 00:01:01,325
It is heavy now.

28
00:01:02,243 --> 00:01:04,373
A push, and it all rolls along.

29
00:01:06,093 --> 00:01:08,963
A trolley is for carrying heavy groceries.

30
00:01:09,533 --> 00:01:11,203
That is its purpose.

31
00:01:15,163 --> 00:01:16,393
Say it with me!

32
00:01:17,107 --> 00:01:19,387
Materials are used to make objects.

33
00:01:19,987 --> 00:01:22,957
Objects are things you use for different purposes.

34
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:26,870
A towel.

35
00:01:27,180 --> 00:01:28,020
Scissors.

36
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:29,360
A raincoat.

37
00:01:29,630 --> 00:01:31,320
Each has its own purpose.

38
00:01:32,562 --> 00:01:35,092
Round one: the question from last time!

39
00:01:35,352 --> 00:01:37,062
Glass, metal, or fabric?

40
00:01:37,352 --> 00:01:38,662
Show me your fingers!

41
00:01:42,131 --> 00:01:43,111
Locked in!

42
00:01:43,239 --> 00:01:43,849
One!

43
00:01:43,989 --> 00:01:44,809
Glass!

44
00:01:44,869 --> 00:01:46,449
I can see all my snacks!

45
00:01:46,502 --> 00:01:46,962
Three.

46
00:01:47,562 --> 00:01:51,062
My fabric bag carries heavy books, and it does not tear.

47
00:01:51,109 --> 00:01:51,889
Two!

48
00:01:51,969 --> 00:01:53,919
The trolleys here are all metal!

49
00:01:54,871 --> 00:01:56,021
Look closer.

50
00:01:56,611 --> 00:01:59,471
The metal trolley, full of heavy groceries.

51
00:01:59,996 --> 00:02:01,776
The metal bars stay straight.

52
00:02:02,346 --> 00:02:03,636
They do not bend.

53
00:02:05,742 --> 00:02:08,052
Now it rolls into the trolley bay.

54
00:02:08,652 --> 00:02:09,422
Clang!

55
00:02:09,992 --> 00:02:11,202
A hard knock.

56
00:02:14,509 --> 00:02:15,529
No crack.

57
00:02:16,149 --> 00:02:17,179
No break.

58
00:02:17,779 --> 00:02:19,059
Metal is strong.

59
00:02:22,855 --> 00:02:25,365
Glass is fragile, but metal is strong.

60
00:02:25,645 --> 00:02:28,865
A glass cup breaks easily when it is dropped, but a metal

61
00:02:28,885 --> 00:02:30,015
cup does not.

62
00:02:31,101 --> 00:02:31,811
Oops.

63
00:02:31,871 --> 00:02:33,181
Bye-bye, snacks!

64
00:02:34,616 --> 00:02:35,646
And fabric?

65
00:02:35,906 --> 00:02:37,666
Pip's bag holds the rice.

66
00:02:37,916 --> 00:02:40,556
But it folds flat: fabric is flexible.

67
00:02:41,338 --> 00:02:42,058
Oh!

68
00:02:42,338 --> 00:02:44,128
A trolley must not bend!

69
00:02:44,254 --> 00:02:45,564
The answer is two.

70
00:02:45,844 --> 00:02:46,644
Metal!

71
00:02:46,924 --> 00:02:47,954
Two fingers?

72
00:02:48,224 --> 00:02:49,434
One finger up!

73
00:02:50,663 --> 00:02:51,813
Say it with me!

74
00:02:52,527 --> 00:02:54,767
Every material has physical properties.

75
00:02:55,277 --> 00:02:58,457
The physical properties of a material allow it to be used in

76
00:02:58,477 --> 00:02:59,707
certain ways.

77
00:03:02,932 --> 00:03:04,862
So glass is a bad material!

78
00:03:04,942 --> 00:03:06,882
Never use glass for anything!

79
00:03:07,003 --> 00:03:08,563
Something is not right.

80
00:03:08,833 --> 00:03:11,013
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

81
00:03:11,293 --> 00:03:12,253
Hold on!

82
00:03:17,766 --> 00:03:18,896
Arms crossed?

83
00:03:19,166 --> 00:03:20,326
One finger up!

84
00:03:20,606 --> 00:03:22,526
Glass is not a bad material.

85
00:03:22,796 --> 00:03:24,356
It depends on the use.

86
00:03:24,706 --> 00:03:25,726
Hold on, Momo!

87
00:03:25,906 --> 00:03:27,836
The fish tank next door is glass!

88
00:03:28,708 --> 00:03:29,838
Look closer.

89
00:03:30,448 --> 00:03:32,618
A glass fish tank, full of water.

90
00:03:33,124 --> 00:03:35,104
We can see every fish clearly.

91
00:03:35,684 --> 00:03:37,314
Glass is transparent.

92
00:03:39,436 --> 00:03:41,196
The shelf under it is dry.

93
00:03:41,776 --> 00:03:43,406
No water passes through.

94
00:03:43,996 --> 00:03:45,596
Glass is waterproof.

95
00:03:46,107 --> 00:03:49,077
For a fish tank, glass is the right material!

96
00:03:52,974 --> 00:03:53,304
Oh!

97
00:03:53,324 --> 00:03:55,084
The same glass.

98
00:03:55,154 --> 00:03:56,474
A different use!

99
00:03:56,820 --> 00:03:57,820
Be the metal!

100
00:03:58,130 --> 00:03:59,110
Shrink down.

101
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:00,320
Quietly.

102
00:04:02,602 --> 00:04:05,722
You are a metal bar, at the bottom of the trolley.

103
00:04:06,443 --> 00:04:08,593
A heavy bag of rice lands on you.

104
00:04:09,363 --> 00:04:10,673
You do not bend.

105
00:04:11,338 --> 00:04:12,528
The wheels roll.

106
00:04:13,328 --> 00:04:15,048
The floor rushes past.

107
00:04:15,781 --> 00:04:16,571
Clang!

108
00:04:17,361 --> 00:04:18,481
A hard knock.

109
00:04:19,321 --> 00:04:20,521
You do not break.

110
00:04:21,361 --> 00:04:22,451
You are strong!

111
00:04:24,728 --> 00:04:26,188
Show me your score hand!

112
00:04:26,468 --> 00:04:27,858
One finger or more?

113
00:04:28,178 --> 00:04:29,538
You beat the Buddies.

114
00:04:29,808 --> 00:04:30,838
Two fingers?

115
00:04:31,118 --> 00:04:32,128
High five!

116
00:04:32,625 --> 00:04:33,955
Did you spot the mynah?

117
00:04:34,275 --> 00:04:36,075
It was on the trolley bay sign!

118
00:04:36,268 --> 00:04:37,417
Here's a fun fact!

119
00:04:37,437 --> 00:04:41,584
Mynahs build their nests from dry grass, twigs, string, and even bits

120
00:04:41,604 --> 00:04:42,489
of plastic!

121
00:04:42,750 --> 00:04:44,030
Tell someone at home!

122
00:04:44,684 --> 00:04:46,884
Let's read today's key words together!

123
00:04:47,174 --> 00:04:47,934
Ready?

124
00:04:48,271 --> 00:04:48,993
Purpose.

125
00:04:50,463 --> 00:04:51,873
Physical properties.

126
00:04:53,695 --> 00:04:54,635
Well done!

127
00:04:55,532 --> 00:04:56,092
Look!

128
00:04:56,262 --> 00:04:58,192
Three water bottles in our trolley!

129
00:04:58,245 --> 00:04:59,395
One plastic.

130
00:04:59,665 --> 00:05:00,695
One glass.

131
00:05:01,015 --> 00:05:01,935
One metal.

132
00:05:02,225 --> 00:05:04,455
The same object, three materials!

133
00:05:04,725 --> 00:05:06,405
Which one is right for school?

134
00:05:06,458 --> 00:05:08,048
Find out in Part Two!

135
00:05:09,108 --> 00:05:10,209
Say it with us!

136
00:05:11,009 --> 00:05:11,759
Ready?

137
00:05:11,882 --> 00:05:12,542
One!

138
00:05:12,882 --> 00:05:13,582
two!

139
00:05:13,887 --> 00:05:15,062
Now you know!
